FreeCORE
========

FreeCORE carries the TrueNAS® CORE 13.3 system forward as an independently
maintained operating system on FreeBSD. It is not affiliated with or endorsed
by iXsystems, Inc. Thanks to the FreeNAS and TrueNAS contributors whose
open-source work made this possible.


Upstream lineage
----------------

This repository begins at a commit from the public upstream repository named in
its README. That upstream history is preserved verbatim: original commits,
original authors, original dates. Every FreeCORE change sits above it as clearly
labelled commits.

To see the entire FreeCORE delta for this repository:

    git log --oneline <base>..HEAD
    git diff <base>..HEAD

The base commit is recorded in the README.


Licensing
---------

FreeCORE does not relicense anything. Each repository keeps the licence it
inherited, and all upstream copyright notices and licence texts are preserved
unchanged. Removing them would be the violation; de-branding a fork means
trademarks come out of user-facing chrome, not that licence headers come out of
source files.

Proprietary and Enterprise-licensed components that were present in upstream
TrueNAS CORE have been removed rather than redistributed. Where callers needed a
surface to keep working, they were replaced with stubs that report the honest
unlicensed, non-iX-hardware state.


